  "id": "Compound::DB01017 - Gene::9376",
  "verbalization": "Minocycline is implicated in the transport of organic anions through Slc22a8, as evidenced by its binding to Slc22a11 and Slc22a7, which in turn participate in organic anion transport. This suggests that Minocycline may influence the activity of Slc22a8 through its interaction with these transporters. The shared involvement of Slc22a8 in organic anion transport across different pathways further supports a potential functional link between Minocycline and Slc22a8. The evidence is consistent with Minocycline acting as a modulator of Slc22a8 function, possibly through the regulation of its associated transporters. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Slc22a8 in organic anion transport and suggests that Minocycline may exert its effects via this route.",
